1
00:00:00,182 --> 00:00:03,147
The SAT reference sheet
mostly covers shapes.

2
00:00:03,932 --> 00:00:07,340
Algebra and advanced math are about
seventy percent of the math section,

3
00:00:07,360 --> 00:00:10,340
and almost none of their
formulas are on it.

4
00:00:10,360 --> 00:00:12,396
There are fifteen you need to know.

5
00:00:12,611 --> 00:00:13,611
Slope.

6
00:00:13,825 --> 00:00:15,325
The quadratic formula.

7
00:00:15,790 --> 00:00:17,037
The circle equation.

8
00:00:17,057 --> 00:00:21,022
And one of them looks so simple that
the trap answer feels exactly right.

9
00:00:21,088 --> 00:00:23,282
That's percent change, formula fourteen,

10
00:00:23,302 --> 00:00:24,372
so stay for it.

11
00:00:24,730 --> 00:00:26,889
First, here's exactly
what is on the sheet,

12
00:00:26,909 --> 00:00:28,802
so you don't waste time memorizing it.

13
00:00:29,122 --> 00:00:33,908
Then all fifteen, with sixteen
quick SAT-style questions.

14
00:00:34,622 --> 00:00:37,373
Keep score, and see if
you can get all sixteen.

15
00:00:37,453 --> 00:00:38,631
Here's the whole sheet.

16
00:00:39,238 --> 00:00:41,524
Area and circumference of a circle.

17
00:00:42,024 --> 00:00:44,238
Area of a rectangle and a triangle.

18
00:00:45,131 --> 00:00:48,987
The Pythagorean theorem, and
the two special right triangles:

19
00:00:49,416 --> 00:00:51,897
thirty, sixty, ninety, and forty-five,

20
00:00:51,917 --> 00:00:53,160
forty-five, ninety.

21
00:00:53,180 --> 00:00:55,839
Volumes of a rectangular prism, cylinder,

22
00:00:55,859 --> 00:00:57,930
sphere, cone, and pyramid.

23
00:00:58,180 --> 00:01:01,552
And three facts: a circle has
three hundred sixty degrees,

24
00:01:01,572 --> 00:01:05,910
or two pi radians, of arc, and a triangle's
angles add up to one hundred eighty

25
00:01:05,930 --> 00:01:06,817
degrees.

26
00:01:06,837 --> 00:01:07,745
That's all of it.

27
00:01:07,765 --> 00:01:09,102
Look those up when you need them.

28
00:01:09,122 --> 00:01:11,122
Everything else, you need to know cold.

29
00:01:11,184 --> 00:01:13,255
Part one, lines.

30
00:01:14,398 --> 00:01:17,949
Formula one is slope: y two minus y one,

31
00:01:17,969 --> 00:01:20,199
over x two minus x one.

32
00:01:20,219 --> 00:01:21,565
Rise over run.

33
00:01:21,585 --> 00:01:22,692
Example.

34
00:01:23,370 --> 00:01:25,779
A line passes through
the points negative two,

35
00:01:25,799 --> 00:01:28,370
seven, and four, negative five.

36
00:01:28,549 --> 00:01:30,244
What is the slope of the line?

37
00:01:30,264 --> 00:01:31,371
Pause and try it.

38
00:01:34,586 --> 00:01:36,959
The change in y is
negative five minus seven,

39
00:01:36,979 --> 00:01:38,443
or negative twelve.

40
00:01:38,622 --> 00:01:40,816
The change in x is four
minus negative two,

41
00:01:40,836 --> 00:01:42,014
or six.

42
00:01:42,085 --> 00:01:43,959
Negative twelve over six is negative two.

43
00:01:43,979 --> 00:01:45,157
The answer is A.

44
00:01:45,200 --> 00:01:47,108
The traps are flipping
it to run over rise,

45
00:01:47,128 --> 00:01:48,736
and losing a negative sign.

46
00:01:49,700 --> 00:01:52,200
Subtract in the same
order on top and bottom.

47
00:01:52,261 --> 00:01:54,510
Formula two is three forms of a line.

48
00:01:54,546 --> 00:01:55,848
Slope-intercept: y equals m x plus b,

49
00:01:55,868 --> 00:01:58,526
where m is the slope and
b is the y intercept.

50
00:01:58,546 --> 00:02:04,776
Point-slope: y minus y one
equals m times x minus x one,

51
00:02:04,796 --> 00:02:06,689
for when you know a point and the slope.

52
00:02:06,740 --> 00:02:10,883
And standard form: A x plus B y equals C.

53
00:02:11,954 --> 00:02:14,275
Its slope is negative A over B.

54
00:02:14,367 --> 00:02:15,688
Example.

55
00:02:15,724 --> 00:02:19,454
A line has a slope of four and
passes through the point three,

56
00:02:19,474 --> 00:02:20,545
one.

57
00:02:20,617 --> 00:02:23,789
What is the y coordinate
of its y intercept?

58
00:02:23,809 --> 00:02:24,916
Pause and try it.

59
00:02:28,131 --> 00:02:29,345
Use point-slope.

60
00:02:29,774 --> 00:02:33,738
y minus one equals four
times x minus three.

61
00:02:33,881 --> 00:02:37,131
That's y minus one equals
four x minus twelve,

62
00:02:37,344 --> 00:02:39,952
so y equals four x minus eleven.

63
00:02:40,773 --> 00:02:43,238
The y intercept is negative eleven.

64
00:02:43,274 --> 00:02:44,881
Formula three.

65
00:02:44,952 --> 00:02:47,202
Parallel lines have equal slopes.

66
00:02:47,524 --> 00:02:50,524
Perpendicular lines have
negative reciprocal slopes:

67
00:02:50,738 --> 00:02:53,167
flip the fraction and change the sign.

68
00:02:53,216 --> 00:02:54,823
Example.

69
00:02:55,573 --> 00:03:00,715
Line p is defined by six x
minus two y equals seven.

70
00:03:01,716 --> 00:03:04,679
Line q is perpendicular to line p.

71
00:03:05,466 --> 00:03:07,538
What is the slope of line q?

72
00:03:07,624 --> 00:03:08,731
Pause and try it.

73
00:03:11,946 --> 00:03:15,891
Line p is in standard form, so
its slope is negative A over B:

74
00:03:15,911 --> 00:03:19,695
negative six over negative
two, which is three.

75
00:03:19,875 --> 00:03:22,981
Flip it and change the
sign: negative one third.

76
00:03:23,803 --> 00:03:25,482
The answer is B.

77
00:03:25,524 --> 00:03:27,167
Three is the parallel slope.

78
00:03:27,523 --> 00:03:30,917
Negative three and positive one
third each do only half the job.

79
00:03:31,009 --> 00:03:32,402
Formula four.

80
00:03:33,402 --> 00:03:36,330
Distance is the square
root of the change in x,

81
00:03:36,616 --> 00:03:39,452
squared, plus the change in y, squared.

82
00:03:39,472 --> 00:03:41,545
That's just the Pythagorean theorem.

83
00:03:41,794 --> 00:03:45,151
And the midpoint averages the
x values and the y values.

84
00:03:45,251 --> 00:03:46,251
Example.

85
00:03:46,287 --> 00:03:49,231
Segment A B has endpoints
A at negative one,

86
00:03:49,251 --> 00:03:51,501
two, and B at five, ten.

87
00:03:52,144 --> 00:03:54,500
What is the length of segment A B?

88
00:03:54,573 --> 00:03:55,680
Pause and try it.

89
00:03:58,895 --> 00:04:00,538
The changes are six and eight.

90
00:04:00,680 --> 00:04:02,625
Six squared plus eight
squared is one hundred,

91
00:04:02,645 --> 00:04:04,609
and the square root of one hundred is ten.

92
00:04:04,859 --> 00:04:06,823
The midpoint is two, six.

93
00:04:06,859 --> 00:04:11,732
In Desmos, type distance, with
the two points in parentheses,

94
00:04:11,752 --> 00:04:13,038
and you get ten.

95
00:04:13,716 --> 00:04:15,423
Midpoint works the same way.

96
00:04:15,443 --> 00:04:17,622
Part two, quadratics.

97
00:04:18,335 --> 00:04:23,030
Formula five: for a x squared
plus b x plus c equals zero,

98
00:04:23,050 --> 00:04:27,566
x equals negative b, plus or minus the
square root of b squared minus four a c,

99
00:04:27,586 --> 00:04:28,872
all over two a.

100
00:04:28,932 --> 00:04:30,218
Example.

101
00:04:30,504 --> 00:04:34,770
Which of the following are the solutions
to two x squared minus four x minus

102
00:04:34,790 --> 00:04:36,111
three equals zero?

103
00:04:36,194 --> 00:04:37,301
Pause and try it.

104
00:04:40,516 --> 00:04:44,730
a is two, b is negative four,
and c is negative three.

105
00:04:45,016 --> 00:04:47,852
Under the root: sixteen plus twenty-four,

106
00:04:47,872 --> 00:04:49,229
which is forty.

107
00:04:49,409 --> 00:04:52,746
So x equals four, plus
or minus root forty,

108
00:04:52,766 --> 00:04:53,909
over four.

109
00:04:53,955 --> 00:04:56,134
Root forty is two root ten.

110
00:04:56,990 --> 00:05:00,935
Divide every term by two:
two, plus or minus root ten,

111
00:05:00,955 --> 00:05:02,026
over two.

112
00:05:02,241 --> 00:05:03,633
The answer is C.

113
00:05:04,562 --> 00:05:10,026
D forgot to divide by two a, and A
used negative four for negative b.

114
00:05:10,100 --> 00:05:14,350
Formula six is the discriminant:
b squared minus four a c.

115
00:05:14,600 --> 00:05:16,902
Positive means two real solutions.

116
00:05:16,922 --> 00:05:18,723
Zero means exactly one.

117
00:05:18,743 --> 00:05:20,207
Negative means none.

118
00:05:20,235 --> 00:05:21,307
Example.

119
00:05:21,450 --> 00:05:25,073
In the equation x squared
plus ten x plus c equals zero,

120
00:05:25,093 --> 00:05:26,521
c is a constant.

121
00:05:27,093 --> 00:05:30,377
If the equation has
exactly one real solution,

122
00:05:30,521 --> 00:05:32,126
what is the value of c?

123
00:05:32,146 --> 00:05:33,253
Pause and try it.

124
00:05:36,468 --> 00:05:39,897
Exactly one solution means
the discriminant is zero.

125
00:05:40,397 --> 00:05:42,948
One hundred minus four c equals zero,

126
00:05:42,968 --> 00:05:44,575
so c is twenty-five.

127
00:05:44,639 --> 00:05:48,261
Desmos shortcut: graph y equals
x squared plus ten x plus c,

128
00:05:48,281 --> 00:05:49,781
and add a slider for c.

129
00:05:49,853 --> 00:05:52,476
The slider only runs from
negative ten to ten at first,

130
00:05:52,496 --> 00:05:54,531
so change its upper limit to fifty.

131
00:05:54,602 --> 00:05:57,332
Then drag until the parabola
just touches the x axis.

132
00:05:57,352 --> 00:05:58,352
That's at twenty-five.

133
00:05:58,670 --> 00:05:59,829
Formula seven is the vertex.

134
00:05:59,849 --> 00:06:03,528
Its x coordinate is negative b over two a.

135
00:06:04,028 --> 00:06:05,706
Plug that in to get y.

136
00:06:05,848 --> 00:06:11,456
And in vertex form, y
equals a times x minus h,

137
00:06:12,456 --> 00:06:16,242
squared, plus k, the vertex is just h,

138
00:06:16,670 --> 00:06:17,275
k.

139
00:06:17,295 --> 00:06:18,616
Example.

140
00:06:18,759 --> 00:06:24,275
What is the vertex of the graph of y
equals two x squared plus twelve x plus

141
00:06:24,295 --> 00:06:25,072
thirteen?

142
00:06:25,092 --> 00:06:26,200
Pause and try it.

143
00:06:29,414 --> 00:06:31,879
Negative twelve over
four is negative three.

144
00:06:32,057 --> 00:06:36,430
Plug it in: eighteen minus thirty-six
plus thirteen is negative five.

145
00:06:36,450 --> 00:06:39,037
The vertex is negative
three, negative five.

146
00:06:39,057 --> 00:06:40,486
The answer is D.

147
00:06:40,530 --> 00:06:44,422
Desmos check: graph it and
click the bottom of the curve.

148
00:06:45,065 --> 00:06:47,137
Desmos labels the vertex for you.

149
00:06:47,200 --> 00:06:51,752
Formula eight: for a x squared
plus b x plus c equals zero,

150
00:06:51,772 --> 00:06:54,252
the sum of the solutions
is negative b over a,

151
00:06:54,272 --> 00:06:56,521
and the product is c over a.

152
00:06:57,343 --> 00:06:58,629
No solving needed.

153
00:06:58,667 --> 00:06:59,881
Example.

154
00:07:00,416 --> 00:07:05,325
What is the product of the solutions
to two x squared plus nine x minus ten

155
00:07:05,345 --> 00:07:06,345
equals zero?

156
00:07:06,432 --> 00:07:07,540
Pause and try it.

157
00:07:10,754 --> 00:07:13,949
c over a is negative ten over
two, which is negative five.

158
00:07:13,969 --> 00:07:15,290
The answer is B.

159
00:07:16,683 --> 00:07:21,396
Negative nine halves is the sum, and
negative ten forgot to divide by a.

160
00:07:21,441 --> 00:07:23,761
Part three, circles and trig.

161
00:07:24,619 --> 00:07:29,421
Formula nine: x minus h,
squared, plus y minus k,

162
00:07:29,441 --> 00:07:32,191
squared, equals r squared.

163
00:07:32,334 --> 00:07:36,334
The center is h, k, and the radius is r.

164
00:07:37,155 --> 00:07:39,922
If the equation comes
expanded, complete the square.

165
00:07:39,942 --> 00:07:41,458
Example.

166
00:07:41,478 --> 00:07:45,958
The equation x squared plus y squared
plus eight x minus two y equals eight

167
00:07:45,978 --> 00:07:48,298
represents a circle in the x y plane.

168
00:07:49,370 --> 00:07:51,014
What is the radius of the circle?

169
00:07:51,063 --> 00:07:52,171
Pause and try it.

170
00:07:55,385 --> 00:07:58,814
Half of eight is four, and
four squared is sixteen.

171
00:07:59,314 --> 00:08:01,115
Half of negative two is negative one,

172
00:08:01,135 --> 00:08:02,813
and that squared is one.

173
00:08:02,850 --> 00:08:05,170
Add sixteen and one to both sides.

174
00:08:05,190 --> 00:08:10,491
Now it's x plus four,
squared, plus y minus one,

175
00:08:10,511 --> 00:08:12,276
squared, equals twenty-five.

176
00:08:12,296 --> 00:08:14,920
The radius is five, not twenty-five.

177
00:08:14,940 --> 00:08:17,955
The answer is C, and the
center is negative four,

178
00:08:17,975 --> 00:08:18,627
one.

179
00:08:18,647 --> 00:08:19,647
Formula ten.

180
00:08:20,968 --> 00:08:23,468
Arcs and sectors are
fractions of the circle.

181
00:08:23,825 --> 00:08:26,682
The fraction is the central
angle over three sixty.

182
00:08:27,253 --> 00:08:29,647
Multiply it by the
circumference for arc length,

183
00:08:29,825 --> 00:08:31,824
or by the area for sector area.

184
00:08:31,894 --> 00:08:33,501
Example.

185
00:08:33,573 --> 00:08:36,394
A circle has a radius of nine centimeters.

186
00:08:37,001 --> 00:08:39,767
What is the area, in square centimeters,

187
00:08:39,787 --> 00:08:42,501
of a sector with a central
angle of forty degrees?

188
00:08:42,597 --> 00:08:43,704
Pause and try it.

189
00:08:46,919 --> 00:08:48,506
Forty over three sixty is one ninth.

190
00:08:48,526 --> 00:08:52,578
The whole area is eighty-one
pi, so the sector is nine pi.

191
00:08:52,598 --> 00:08:53,919
The answer is B.

192
00:08:53,955 --> 00:08:56,634
Two pi is the arc length,
which is the common mix-up.

193
00:08:56,749 --> 00:09:00,285
If the angle is in radians,
compare it to two pi instead.

194
00:09:00,318 --> 00:09:01,461
Formula eleven.

195
00:09:02,317 --> 00:09:06,512
Soh-cah-toa: sine is
opposite over hypotenuse,

196
00:09:06,532 --> 00:09:10,547
cosine is adjacent over hypotenuse,
and tangent is opposite over adjacent.

197
00:09:10,567 --> 00:09:13,175
Always measured from the
angle the question names.

198
00:09:13,216 --> 00:09:14,216
Example.

199
00:09:14,359 --> 00:09:18,538
In right triangle X Y Z,
angle Z is the right angle.

200
00:09:18,859 --> 00:09:23,787
X Z is twenty-four, Y Z is
seven, and X Y is twenty-five.

201
00:09:24,287 --> 00:09:26,394
What is the value of cosine of X?

202
00:09:26,450 --> 00:09:27,557
Pause and try it.

203
00:09:30,772 --> 00:09:33,985
From angle X, the adjacent
side is twenty-four,

204
00:09:34,128 --> 00:09:36,343
and the hypotenuse is twenty-five.

205
00:09:36,593 --> 00:09:39,502
So cosine of X is
twenty-four over twenty-five.

206
00:09:39,522 --> 00:09:42,272
The answer is C.

207
00:09:42,378 --> 00:09:44,699
Seven over twenty-five is sine of X.

208
00:09:44,783 --> 00:09:49,585
Now notice: from angle Y, sine is
also twenty-four over twenty-five.

209
00:09:49,605 --> 00:09:50,640
That's the rule.

210
00:09:50,747 --> 00:09:54,835
Sine of x equals cosine
of ninety degrees minus x,

211
00:09:54,855 --> 00:09:57,497
because the two acute
angles add up to ninety.

212
00:09:57,575 --> 00:09:58,932
Example.

213
00:09:59,396 --> 00:10:03,090
If sine of x degrees equals
cosine of thirty-two degrees,

214
00:10:03,110 --> 00:10:07,038
and x is between zero and
ninety, what is the value of x?

215
00:10:07,070 --> 00:10:08,177
Pause and try it.

216
00:10:11,392 --> 00:10:13,300
Ninety minus thirty-two is fifty-eight.

217
00:10:13,320 --> 00:10:18,284
To check in Desmos, switch
to degrees in graph settings,

218
00:10:18,605 --> 00:10:22,569
then type sine of fifty-eight
and cosine of thirty-two.

219
00:10:22,856 --> 00:10:23,927
Same decimal.

220
00:10:23,973 --> 00:10:25,901
Part four, exponents.

221
00:10:26,900 --> 00:10:29,080
Formula twelve is a set of rules.

222
00:10:29,330 --> 00:10:31,544
Multiplying, add the exponents.

223
00:10:31,937 --> 00:10:33,973
Dividing, subtract them.

224
00:10:34,150 --> 00:10:36,437
Power of a power, multiply them.

225
00:10:36,937 --> 00:10:38,845
A negative exponent means one over.

226
00:10:38,865 --> 00:10:42,258
And in a fraction exponent, the top is
the power and the bottom is the root.

227
00:10:42,329 --> 00:10:43,309
Example.

228
00:10:43,329 --> 00:10:47,309
Which expression is equivalent to
the quantity three x to the fourth,

229
00:10:47,329 --> 00:10:50,380
squared, times x to the negative five,

230
00:10:50,400 --> 00:10:52,007
where x is not zero?

231
00:10:52,064 --> 00:10:53,172
Pause and try it.

232
00:10:56,386 --> 00:10:58,671
Squaring gives nine x to the eighth.

233
00:10:59,029 --> 00:11:01,009
Then multiply by x to the negative five,

234
00:11:01,029 --> 00:11:05,152
so add the exponents:
eight minus five is three.

235
00:11:05,172 --> 00:11:07,208
That's nine x cubed.

236
00:11:07,457 --> 00:11:09,421
The answer is A.

237
00:11:10,029 --> 00:11:12,172
C doubled the three
instead of squaring it.

238
00:11:12,206 --> 00:11:13,813
Formula thirteen.

239
00:11:14,492 --> 00:11:17,329
Growth: y equals a times
the quantity one plus r,

240
00:11:17,349 --> 00:11:18,349
to the t.

241
00:11:18,885 --> 00:11:21,135
For decay, it's one minus r.

242
00:11:21,348 --> 00:11:24,634
a is the starting amount, and
r is the percent as a decimal.

243
00:11:24,677 --> 00:11:25,550
Example.

244
00:11:25,570 --> 00:11:28,443
A machine was worth five thousand
dollars when it was bought,

245
00:11:28,463 --> 00:11:31,534
and its value decreases
by ten percent each year.

246
00:11:32,033 --> 00:11:35,033
Which function gives
its value V, in dollars,

247
00:11:35,498 --> 00:11:37,463
t years after it was bought?

248
00:11:37,532 --> 00:11:38,640
Pause and try it.

249
00:11:41,854 --> 00:11:44,854
Losing ten percent means
keeping ninety percent,

250
00:11:44,926 --> 00:11:47,192
so the multiplier is point nine.

251
00:11:47,212 --> 00:11:49,890
The answer is D.

252
00:11:49,961 --> 00:11:53,426
B keeps only ten percent, C is growth,

253
00:11:53,497 --> 00:11:54,844
and A is linear.

254
00:11:54,864 --> 00:11:57,916
After two years, the machine is
worth four thousand fifty dollars,

255
00:11:57,936 --> 00:11:59,293
not four thousand.

256
00:11:59,400 --> 00:12:02,150
Each year takes ten percent
of a smaller amount.

257
00:12:02,614 --> 00:12:06,593
In Desmos, use x for t, define f of x,

258
00:12:06,613 --> 00:12:08,257
and type f of two to check.

259
00:12:08,320 --> 00:12:10,749
Part five, percents and stats.

260
00:12:11,819 --> 00:12:15,122
Formula fourteen: percent
change is new minus old,

261
00:12:15,142 --> 00:12:16,999
over old, times one hundred.

262
00:12:17,391 --> 00:12:20,086
From forty dollars to
thirty-four is a six-dollar drop,

263
00:12:20,106 --> 00:12:23,142
and six over forty is a
fifteen percent decrease.

264
00:12:23,175 --> 00:12:25,389
The SAT also runs it backward.

265
00:12:25,746 --> 00:12:26,583
Example.

266
00:12:26,603 --> 00:12:31,067
After a twenty percent discount, a
jacket costs forty-eight dollars.

267
00:12:31,424 --> 00:12:33,460
What was the original price of the jacket?

268
00:12:33,516 --> 00:12:34,623
Pause and try it.

269
00:12:37,838 --> 00:12:40,210
Twenty percent off means
you pay eighty percent.

270
00:12:40,230 --> 00:12:42,139
Point eight times the
price is forty-eight,

271
00:12:42,159 --> 00:12:44,516
so the price is sixty dollars.

272
00:12:44,909 --> 00:12:47,266
The answer is C.

273
00:12:47,298 --> 00:12:50,028
The trap is B, adding twenty
percent of forty-eight.

274
00:12:50,048 --> 00:12:53,492
But the discount came
off the original price,

275
00:12:53,512 --> 00:12:54,725
not the sale price.

276
00:12:54,797 --> 00:12:58,833
Formula fifteen: the mean is
the sum divided by the count.

277
00:12:59,333 --> 00:13:03,547
The version the SAT really wants
is total equals mean times count.

278
00:13:03,657 --> 00:13:04,657
Example.

279
00:13:04,943 --> 00:13:07,566
The mean of a student's five
test scores is eighty-two.

280
00:13:07,586 --> 00:13:12,636
What score on a sixth test would make
the mean of all six scores equal to

281
00:13:12,656 --> 00:13:13,463
eighty-four?

282
00:13:13,483 --> 00:13:14,590
Pause and try it.

283
00:13:17,805 --> 00:13:21,141
Five scores averaging eighty-two
total four hundred ten.

284
00:13:21,161 --> 00:13:24,178
Six scores averaging eighty-four
total five hundred four.

285
00:13:24,198 --> 00:13:26,055
The difference is ninety-four.

286
00:13:27,448 --> 00:13:29,391
Whenever values are added or removed,

287
00:13:29,411 --> 00:13:30,625
switch to totals.

288
00:13:30,674 --> 00:13:33,923
On test day, trigger words
tell you which formula to use.

289
00:13:34,173 --> 00:13:36,154
Perpendicular: negative reciprocal.

290
00:13:36,174 --> 00:13:39,281
Exactly one solution: discriminant.

291
00:13:39,924 --> 00:13:43,439
Sum or product of the
solutions: negative b over a,

292
00:13:43,459 --> 00:13:44,710
or c over a.

293
00:13:45,067 --> 00:13:47,246
Maximum or minimum: vertex.

294
00:13:47,282 --> 00:13:50,512
Center or radius: complete the square.

295
00:13:50,532 --> 00:13:53,155
Percent per year: one plus or minus r,

296
00:13:53,175 --> 00:13:54,175
to the t.

297
00:13:54,495 --> 00:13:56,512
A mean with a value added or removed:

298
00:13:56,532 --> 00:13:57,532
totals.

299
00:13:57,602 --> 00:14:00,245
And if it's on the reference
sheet, just open the sheet.

300
00:14:00,305 --> 00:14:02,928
That's all fifteen on one screen.

301
00:14:02,948 --> 00:14:04,591
Pause here if you want a screenshot.

302
